    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2P7a9RyQJJ3nUppAmgcFeXc)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: based on `main`, no dependencies.\n- Touches only `sp-batch-report-view` (doc, `.el`, test); no open PR edits those files (checked #537, #455, #446, #443, #171, #125).\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Branch name could not carry the PR number (cloud session limit); the number is #538.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** padding between the entries of the batch report, and alternating text colors by row and column so cells form a checkerboard.\n- **Note:** there is no `sp-batch-process` in the code; the UI is the special-mode view in `sp-batch-report-view` (the report that `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-*` and similar commands open).\n- **Checkerboard** (tables only):\n  - `sp-batch-report-cell-even`: inherits `default`.\n  - `sp-batch-report-cell-odd`: inherits `font-lock-constant-face` (theme-aware, light and dark), `shadow` without colors.\n  - Cell (row, column) uses the even face when row + column is even, so no two neighbours across or down share a color.\n  - Link faces and the dropped strike-through stay on top; the header keeps `sp-batch-report-column`.\n- **Padding:** `sp-batch-report-row-padding` (default 0.5): height of a blank line after each entry; nil or 0 for none. Applies to tables and lists.\n- Docs: new bullet section \"Checkerboard colors and padding\" in `sp-batch-report-view.org`; `.el` re-tangled.\n- Tests (Emacs 29.3): 2 new, 23 of 23 pass in `sp-batch-report-view-test.el`.\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh`: the module differs only by this change (committed). Other drift it printed in my container (`sp-litnotes-meta`, `sp-batch-report-test`) is an Org-version artifact and was not committed.\n- No CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Not run:** the GUI, light and dark themes.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-*` (any report with a table): neighbouring cells across and down alternate colors\n- [ ] Switch between a light and a dark theme: both colors stay readable\n- [ ] A small gap separates the entries; `n`/`p` still move row by row\n- [ ] `d` on a row: strike-through still shows over the alternating colors; `u` restores\n- [ ] `(setq sp-batch-report-row-padding nil)` then `g`: no gaps\n- [ ] `M-x customize-face sp-batch-report-cell-odd`: the change shows after `g`\n- [ ] Regression: TAB folds a section, links in cells still open with RET, resizing the frame re-wraps the tables\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the local branch: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/project-thread-76fy32`.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDPTK7chW7brUzTypK)_",
